{"id": "EUVD-2026-76667", "enisaUuid": "5bcfb98c-c942-313b-b1d3-c30e3db37d94", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmm/migrate_device: clear stale mapping after freeing swapcache\n\n__migrate_device_pages() reads the folio mapping before calling\nfolio_free_swap().  When folio_free_swap() succeeds, the folio is removed\nfrom the swap cache, but the saved mapping still points to swap_space.\n\nPassing the stale mapping to folio_migrate_mapping() makes it use the\nmapped-folio path for a folio that is no longer in swapcache.  It can then\noperate on swap_space.i_pages with invalid reference accounting,\neventually triggering a folio reference count BUG.\n\nAfter a successful split, nr still contains the number of pages in the\noriginal large folio, although each resulting page is now a separate\norder-0 folio.  Reset nr to 1 so each split folio is processed separately,\nincluding its own swapcache removal and mapping lookup.\n\nRefresh the saved mapping after folio_free_swap() so the current folio\nstate is used during migration.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:46:58", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:48:34", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/92db780dd644590c751246187e1229d5ac2e5544", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4fa91f7bbc4135240b67daac03fc17d9e180a331", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8ffedc6573a665cdc31ebe47eae7b32b78d0df83", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/34a00895d032a414830d41106a09329ae6c251b6"], "aliases": ["GHSA-f448-r8g9-p8j7", "CVE-2026-89755"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0b8ecb71-c45e-3dd9-9537-5e0f93d733e6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "df263d9a7dffee94ca5391120ee3b0587efa07f1 <34a00895d032a414830d41106a09329ae6c251b6"}, {"id": "12913774-57f9-39f1-b126-0aff56f474aa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "df263d9a7dffee94ca5391120ee3b0587efa07f1 <4fa91f7bbc4135240b67daac03fc17d9e180a331"}, {"id": "3cf29f7d-dad1-33d2-8af1-50a5300871dd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "4cd0ea4b-4ed6-3744-a73f-446e9d998d43", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "4e091a5d-19f3-30e5-a06a-def44bb5ccd6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6"}, {"id": "652fbf98-ba95-3f2b-8087-864a82e4a3ba", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "8bac894c-5ebb-3723-b75e-3d2b96b6f4a9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "8bd6c372-5ee3-3a37-a3ba-0f6322fc1743", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "dbd58866-f9b9-313c-89ab-46bf1135c76c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "df263d9a7dffee94ca5391120ee3b0587efa07f1 <92db780dd644590c751246187e1229d5ac2e5544"}, {"id": "f7ef873a-805f-3f31-8a61-ec61973d46d0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "df263d9a7dffee94ca5391120ee3b0587efa07f1 <8ffedc6573a665cdc31ebe47eae7b32b78d0df83"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "bd921521-ed93-35e8-b8c6-dda007b03075", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}